      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Declared-Value Transit Marine Insurance Tariffs &amp; GST Compliance for Car Transportation Charges From Delhi To Guwahati</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a car from Delhi to Guwahati involves considering various factors, including tax structures and insurance premiums. In India, tax structures involve two main components: standard Goods and Services Tax (GST) and declared-value transit marine insurance. Let's break down these components:</p>

<h3>GST Rates</h3>
<p>GST is a value-added tax that is applied at multiple stages of production and consumption. For car transportation services, the standard GST rate is 18%. However, there is an option for a reduced 5% GST rate when the car transportation service is considered a "composite supply," which involves multiple services provided under a single contract.</p>

<h3>Declared-Value Transit Marine Insurance</h3>
<p>Transit marine insurance is essential for protecting your car during the transportation process. Declared-value insurance is common, which means you can opt for a coverage based on the declared value of your car. The insurance premium is typically around 1.5% to 3% of the declared value.</p>

<h3>Statutory Insurance Premiums</h3>
<p>The statutory insurance premiums for car transportation services usually range between 1.5% to 3% of the declared value. This insurance covers the car during transportation and protects it against any damages or loss. The insurance premium is typically included in the overall transportation cost.</p>

<h3>Insurance Coverage Details</h3>
