    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">These transporters might claim that the pickup or drop-off address has a long distance to reach the transporter, which results in extra labor costs or fuel expenses. However, a well-planned route should account for such factors and shouldn't necessarily lead to a long carry.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Toll Taxes:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Some dishonest transporters might claim that certain roads or highways have tolls, which need to be paid by the customer. While tolls may exist, the transporter should have accounted for them in the initial quote and should not charge extra once the job starts.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To safeguard yourself from such deceptive practices, it is essential to rely on written binding quotes provided by the car transportation company.</p>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Transparency:</strong> A reliable transporter will provide a clear and transparent quote detailing all charges involved, including floor elevation, long carries, and toll taxes. This ensures that there are no hidden fees or unexpected costs at the time of delivery.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Binding Nature:</strong> A binding quote guarantees that the provided rates will remain fixed throughout the entire process, protecting customers from price hikes or additional charges. This binding nature adds a sense of security and trustworthiness to the service provider.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Competitive Rates:</strong> Transporters with a solid reputation will typically provide fair rates without inflating costs for dubious reasons. By comparing quotes from multiple companies, customers can identify the most reasonable and trustworthy transporter.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p>When searching for a reliable car transportation service, it is crucial to seek written binding quotes to ensure a stress-free and transparent experience. Here's how:</p>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>1. Comprehensive Quote: A binding quote covers all aspects of the transportation process, including floor elevation, long carries, and toll taxes.</span></li>

		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>2. Fixed Costs: The binding nature of the quote guarantees that the rates provided will remain unchanged, eliminating the risk of surprise charges at the final stages of the service.</span></li></ul></div>
